An '''empty review''' or '''fake review''' is a review of a card in [[Anki]] where you just press "Good" without thinking it through.

This is most useful when reviewing newly-created [[big card]]s -- there, you might have just spent a lot of time making the card in the first place, so immediately doing a review is not helpful. In this case, the empty review only makes sense when the [[graduating interval]] is large enough.

